#! rate=44118 block=128 tracks=4
# 18 Undo while playing. usnap stores the state under an id; ucommit drops a
# snapshot equal to the current state; uswap restores one id and stores the
# current state under another (undo and redo); a dropped id restores nothing.
# Tempo is part of the snapshot. Undo keeps the transport, but it wraps each
# playhead by the clip length, not by the loop end: track 1 has a window at
# steps 16-31, and after the undo its playhead lands below the window and
# plays step 10, which is outside it (a Movy defect; see the README).
@0 tog 0 0 60 100
@0 tog 0 4 62 100
@0 tog 1 10 55 100
@0 tog 1 20 57 100
@0 loop 1 16 16
@0 play
@10000 usnap 1
@10000 tog 0 8 64 100
@10000 bpm 15000
@10000 ucommit 1
@20000 usnap 3
@20000 ucommit 3
@45000 uswap 1 2
@70000 uswap 2 4
@100000 uswap 3 5
@110000 stop
